      }
     },
     "kind": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
       "tsconfig",
       "jsconfig",
       "other"
      ]
     },
     "extendsResolved": {
      "type": "array",
      "maxItems": 64,
      "minItems": 0,
      "items": {
       "$ref": "#/$defs/CanonicalPath"
      },
      "x-opensip-order": "sequence",
      "description": "The ORDERED resolved extends edges of this node, in the order the config declares them. TypeScript 5.0 supports multiple entries in `extends` and a LATER entry wins, so precedence is the array order and must be retained: an unordered set or a single edge cannot represent an ordinary modern configuration. Empty means this node extends nothing. Repeated edges are retained; this is a sequence, not a set."
     }
    }
   },
   "x-opensip-order": {
    "by": [
     "path"
    ]
   }
  }
 },
 "description": "The resolved tsconfig/jsconfig extends graph a TypeScript universe commits to. entryConfigPath is the SELECTED root config the program was opened with, null exactly when the configuration was synthesized; nodes is every config file actually read, strictly ascending and unique by path, each carrying its inventoried snapshot digest, its kind and its ORDERED resolved extends edges with later-wins precedence. configOrigin is derived from the ENTRY node kind, never from the whole set: a jsconfig.json that extends a shared base.json is a jsconfig program. Every node must be reachable from the entry, every edge must name another node, and the edge graph must be acyclic. tsconfigGraphHash is the raw SHA-256 of C(this record). A selected entry whose kind is other represents an explicitly selected custom-named TypeScript configuration and derives configOrigin tsconfig."
}
